# Neutral Spanish: no "vosotros", and no vocabulary that belongs to one country
# rather than the language. The interface addresses the listener as "tú", which
# is what the English does by using the imperative and no pronoun at all.
#
# The menu accelerators -- the letter after "&" -- were reassigned rather than
# translated: they have to be unique within one menu and they have to be a
# letter the Spanish label actually contains. None of them sits on an accented
# vowel, which several platforms underline badly.
#
